	<methods>
		<method name="articulation_add_link">
			<return type="int" />
			<param index="0" name="articulation" type="RID" />
			<param index="1" name="parent_index" type="int" />
			<param index="2" name="parent_frame" type="Transform3D" />
			<param index="3" name="child_frame" type="Transform3D" />
			<param index="4" name="joint_type" type="int" />
			<param index="5" name="density" type="float" />
			<param index="6" name="box_half_extents" type="Vector3" />
			<description>
				Adds a link and returns its 0-based index. [param parent_index] -1 creates the base link (world-posed via [param child_frame]; [param joint_type] ignored). Otherwise [param child_frame] is the link pose relative to its parent and [param parent_frame] the inbound joint anchor in the parent link's frame. [param joint_type]: 0 FIX, 1 PRISMATIC, 2 REVOLUTE, 3 REVOLUTE_UNWRAPPED, 4 SPHERICAL. Each link gets a default box collision shape ([param box_half_extents]); mass properties derive from it at [param density]. Replace the shape with [method articulation_set_link_shape].
			</description>
		</method>
		<method name="articulation_create">
			<return type="RID" />
			<description>
				Creates a reduced-coordinate articulation (PhysX [code]PxArticulationReducedCoordinate[/code]) and returns its RID. Configure links, drives and flags, then attach it to a space with [method articulation_set_space]. Links must be added before the articulation joins a space.
			</description>
		</method>
